; ..\BSW\NvM\NvM.c	  2145   \REASON COV_MSR_MISRA
; ..\BSW\NvM\NvM.c	  2146  
; ..\BSW\NvM\NvM.c	  2147  \ID COV_NVM_COVEREDINOTHERCFG
; ..\BSW\NvM\NvM.c	  2148   \ACCEPT TX
; ..\BSW\NvM\NvM.c	  2149   \ACCEPT TX tx tx
; ..\BSW\NvM\NvM.c	  2150   \ACCEPT TF tf tf xf
; ..\BSW\NvM\NvM.c	  2151   \REASON Some configurations do not provide all functionalities required to go through all code branches. But the correctness of the affected code
; ..\BSW\NvM\NvM.c	  2152           is ensured via tests in other configurations, which covers the code completely.
; ..\BSW\NvM\NvM.c	  2153  
; ..\BSW\NvM\NvM.c	  2154  \ID COV_NVM_NOCRCDUMMYHANDLER
; ..\BSW\NvM\NvM.c	  2155   \ACCEPT X
; ..\BSW\NvM\NvM.c	  2156   \REASON All NvM CRC handlers have the same structure: they provide a function to calculate, compare and copy data. For blocks
; ..\BSW\NvM\NvM.c	  2157           without CRC the NvM uses a dummy CRC handler, which simply does nothing, but exists to simplify CRC handling: NvM does not have to
; ..\BSW\NvM\NvM.c	  2158           check whether the block has a CRC each time, the assigned CRC handler does it. The uncovered function...
; ..\BSW\NvM\NvM.c	  2159  
; ..\BSW\NvM\NvM.c	  2160  \ID COV_NVM_KILLWRITEALL
; ..\BSW\NvM\NvM.c	  2161   \ACCEPT TF tf tx
; ..\BSW\NvM\NvM.c	  2162   \ACCEPT TX
; ..\BSW\NvM\NvM.c	  2163   \ACCEPT XF
; ..\BSW\NvM\NvM.c	  2164   \ACCEPT XF tf xf
; ..\BSW\NvM\NvM.c	  2165   \REASON All affected code parts belong to NvM_KillWriteAll handling and are currently not testable (NvM processing is not interruptible on required
; ..\BSW\NvM\NvM.c	  2166           points). There are two not covered situations:
; ..\BSW\NvM\NvM.c	  2167           1. NvM isn't processing any block yet or any more (not started or nearly done NvM_WriteAll)
; ..\BSW\NvM\NvM.c	  2168           2. NvM is processing a block and shall abort directly before or after passing the block to underlying modules
; ..\BSW\NvM\NvM.c	  2169  
; ..\BSW\NvM\NvM.c	  2170  \ID COV_NVM_APICFGCLASS
; ..\BSW\NvM\NvM.c	  2171   \ACCEPT TX tf tx
; ..\BSW\NvM\NvM.c	  2172   \ACCEPT TF tf tx
; ..\BSW\NvM\NvM.c	  2173   \ACCEPT TF tx tf
; ..\BSW\NvM\NvM.c	  2174   \ACCEPT TF tx tf tf
; ..\BSW\NvM\NvM.c	  2175   \ACCEPT XF
; ..\BSW\NvM\NvM.c	  2176   \REASON NvM supports three API configuration classes: 3 includes all functionality, 2 removes some functionality and 1 is the smallest
; ..\BSW\NvM\NvM.c	  2177           NvM functionality with only multi block requests. Because of the missing functionalities it is not possible to cover all
; ..\BSW\NvM\NvM.c	  2178           branches. Also some NvM block configuration does not make sense here - e.g. block without permanent RAM will not be processed
; ..\BSW\NvM\NvM.c	  2179           and are responsible for uncovered code.
